(6365083, 941808, 92577, '<td valign="top">Whenever I get a disappointing score (all too frequently) I would love to have someone give their opinion of why.<br/>    I think in your shot the first impression would be that it appears to be out of focus. I know that one of her eyes (the furthest away) is in focus but because of the low camera angle, there''s a lot of OOF face before you get to the eyes. (I''m no expert but a rule of thumb in portraiture suggests shooting at eye level or slightly above.) <br/>Secondly there is no connection between the model and the viewer - she is looking away with an almost expressionless face. <br/>    And finally the lighting is a little harsh.  <br/>Hope this was helpful. I gave this a 6 BTW.<br/> <br/>David<br/></td>', 'Whenever I get a disappointing score (all too frequently) I would love to have someone give their opinion of why.    I think in your shot the first impression would be that it appears to be out of focus. I know that one of her eyes (the furthest away) is in focus but because of the low camera angle, there''s a lot of OOF face before you get to the eyes. (I''m no expert but a rule of thumb in portraiture suggests shooting at eye level or slightly above.) Secondly there is no connection between the model and the viewer - she is looking away with an almost expressionless face.     And finally the lighting is a little harsh.  Hope this was helpful. I gave this a 6 BTW. David', '2011-03-28 05:14:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(6365086, 941563, 117474, '<td valign="top">Heh. Yeah. <br/>I think I prefer yours, though. There was an issue with bracketing in mine and the shadows were too dark, so I had to go heavy on processing to get even levels everywhere. <br/></td>', 'Heh. Yeah. I think I prefer yours, though. There was an issue with bracketing in mine and the shadows were too dark, so I had to go heavy on processing to get even levels everywhere. ', '2011-03-28 05:17:49.000000', NULL, 0),
