(6371729, 941788, 68947, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by posthumous:</b></div><hr/><i> hey, is that a shoehorn?? hahaha </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>LOL Don...yeah, I guess you could say that it was ROFL!!  <br/> <br/>Actually, it was the end result of spending a couple of hours using that oriental spoon above the wine glass to capture some form of interesting "splash shot" that''s so famous to DPC ribboners. <br/> <br/>In giving up, I simply dropped the oriental soup spoon into the glass and shot it.  It amazed me that the bubbles had formed in the water and on the botton of the glass and sides.  In complete frustration out of the hours that I''d spent on this stupid shot, I entered it anyway.  <br/> <br/>I should really have just done this in the first place! LOL ;)  It would have saved time and a mess and still ended up being better score wise than when I have really tried hard!  <br/> <br/>Thanks for the comments and interest.  Made my day. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by posthumous: hey, is that a shoehorn?? hahaha   LOL Don...yeah, I guess you could say that it was ROFL!!   Actually, it was the end result of spending a couple of hours using that oriental spoon above the wine glass to capture some form of interesting "splash shot" that''s so famous to DPC ribboners.  In giving up, I simply dropped the oriental soup spoon into the glass and shot it.  It amazed me that the bubbles had formed in the water and on the botton of the glass and sides.  In complete frustration out of the hours that I''d spent on this stupid shot, I entered it anyway.   I should really have just done this in the first place! LOL ;)  It would have saved time and a mess and still ended up being better score wise than when I have really tried hard!   Thanks for the comments and interest.  Made my day. :)', '2011-04-03 18:42:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6374402, 941823, 16106, '<td valign="top">How this got any votes below 5 amazes me, cause you nailed the challenge with a lovely image. The only possible improvement would be to widen the white background to bring it around the sides to lessen the dark lines reflected  along the sides of the glass.</td>', 'How this got any votes below 5 amazes me, cause you nailed the challenge with a lovely image. The only possible improvement would be to widen the white background to bring it around the sides to lessen the dark lines reflected  along the sides of the glass.', '2011-04-05 01:50:07.000000', NULL, 0),
